{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context\n\nThe remote gate is refs/reconciler/gate. Older binaries require a non-empty gated_mode string and fail closed on unknown formats. Retiring the mode ladder therefore needs an additive, rollback-safe blob rather than a new-only schema. The writer will retain gated_mode: reconcile-check while adding paused, reason, who, and paused_at. The pre-change decoder ignores the additive fields and continues to block every mutating legacy mode. The read-only legacy reconcile-check path remains allowed and may report green while paused; that is intentional because it cannot mutate Jira or ticket state.\n\nThere is no duration or automatic expiry in this change. An --until field would diverge old and new readers and could silently unpause only part of the fleet, so it is explicitly out of scope. Pause remains active until an operator resumes it.\n\nThe existing set_gate and clear_gate ref writers already use expected-old-oid CAS. The new operator surface must preserve that mechanism: a rejected CAS is surfaced as a clean conflict with the current remote state; it is never retried blindly or allowed to clobber another operator.\n\nA live error-path bug is included because it crosses the same seam: check_phase_gate runs before the reconciler try block today, so a corrupt gate escapes as a traceback. Move the call inside the protected path and emit a clean exit 4 with the recovery command. Do not rename check_phase_gate in this ticket.\n\n## Operator behavior\n\n- rebar bridge pause REASON requires a nonblank reason and writes the additive dual-format blob.\n- Pausing an already-paused bridge is idempotent only when the requested reason matches; it reports the existing pause without changing who or paused_at. A different reason refuses with the current state so provenance is not overwritten accidentally.\n- rebar bridge resume clears the gate through the same CAS seam. Resuming an unpaused bridge exits 0 with a notice.\n- Missing origin refuses loudly; CAS conflict exits nonzero with the re-read remote state; corrupt state exits 4 with recovery guidance.\n- .github/workflows/reconcile-bridge.yml adds an explicit paused exit-4 notice arm before the generic error arm, so scheduled pauses do not make CI red.\n\n## Compatibility and tests\n\nUse expand-contract ordering: the additive reader and dual-format writer ship together, and every new blob is fed to a verbatim pre-change decoder. Prove gated_mode is still a real legacy Mode member. Exercise pause/resume through the real bridge CLI, including blank reason, already-paused same/different reason, unpaused resume, missing remote, CAS conflict, corrupt blob, and exact remote ref state. Assert the old reconcile --mode surface still reads the blob: mutating modes remain blocked while read-only reconcile-check remains allowed. Assert the workflow maps paused exit 4 to notice and preserves all existing success/error mappings.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] Every new gate blob carries paused, reason, who, paused_at and retains gated_mode: reconcile-check.\n- [ ] A vendored pre-change decoder accepts every blob the new writer can emit, and tests prove mutating legacy modes stay blocked while read-only reconcile-check remains allowed.\n- [ ] rebar bridge pause REASON and rebar bridge resume are the only supported write path; no operator needs git plumbing.\n- [ ] Blank reasons are rejected; same-reason re-pause is idempotent without metadata loss; different-reason re-pause refuses; resume while unpaused is a successful notice.\n- [ ] Existing expected-old-oid CAS protects pause/resume, and a conflict surfaces the current remote state without blind retry or overwrite.\n- [ ] A corrupt gate blob produces clean exit 4 with recovery guidance, not a traceback.\n- [ ] Pause detects a missing remote and refuses rather than reporting local-only success.\n- [ ] The scheduled workflow treats paused exit 4 as a notice and preserves prior exit mappings.\n- [ ] No --until, automatic expiry, or new-only blob value ships."}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1786207806352289001,"uuid":"c70bb5ad-73f1-41d4-b84e-0c3ec233576a"}